Z||000000||87ECO5||04-07-2000||01:43 PM||||Wasn't sure how to search on this topic.  If it's already been covered, please direct me to the thread.<P>I'm planning to add the electric trunk release and power mirrors to my economy coupe but I have a question about the panels that surround these accessories' switches.<P>On "loaded" cars, the right side of the gauge pod has a panel with two openings for the trunk release and rear defrost and the center console panel has three openings for the two power window switches and power mirror switch.  On "stripped" cars (like mine), both panels are solid.<P>My question is ... did they make panels with configurations that weren't "all or nothing?"  In my case, I'll need a gauge pod panel with a single opening (either top or bottom) and a center console panel with the center opening only for the power mirrors.<P>If they made these different configurations, then I'll post a "WANT TO PURCHASE" thread in the mall section.<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||87PegasusGT||04-07-2000||03:05 PM||||Well, I have the mirrors, and trunk, but no defroster, so I know loaded doesn't mean everything.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-07-2000||03:33 PM||||look in the ogre cave for installation details, see link at bottom of page.<P>yes they made multiple switch brackets. There are a total of 4 diferant ones. In your case you can just as easy use the one for the cars that are rear defog w/o trunk. The switches are the same as far as mounting goes. <P>blank<BR>both<BR>trunk/no rear defog<BR>rear defog/no trunk (These are a bit more common I think.)||||reg||1
